| **Example**     | Combining data from CRM, ERP, and external databases to create a comprehensive view of customer interactions. | Converting raw transaction data into standardized formats or aggregating sales data by month. | Centralizing customer data from different departments into a single customer database to ensure data consistency. |

This tabular view provides a clear comparison of integration, transformation, and consolidation, highlighting their respective definitions, purposes, processes, and examples in data engineering.



